# 🤖 AI Worker Burnout & Attrition – End-to-End ML Platform (Microsoft Fabric)

## 📌 Overview

This project demonstrates a fully orchestrated **end-to-end Data Engineering & Machine Learning platform** built in **Microsoft Fabric**.

It covers the complete lifecycle from raw data ingestion to automated model retraining and business-facing predictions in Power BI.

The goal of this project was to simulate a production-ready analytical ML system using modern data platform patterns:

* Medallion Architecture (Bronze / Silver / Gold)
* Spark ML Pipelines
* Model persistence & batch inference
* Orchestrated retraining
* BI consumption layer

---

## 🏗 Architecture

```
Raw CSV (Bronze)
        ↓
Data Cleaning & Validation (Silver)
        ↓
Feature Engineering Pipeline
        ↓
Model Training (LogReg + Random Forest)
        ↓
Batch Inference
        ↓
Gold Prediction Table
        ↓
Power BI Dashboard
```

### Medallion Layers

**Bronze**

* Raw dataset ingestion
* Immutable source table

**Silver**

* Schema enforcement
* Data quality validation
* Business feature enrichment
* Clean, analytics-ready table

**Gold**

* ML predictions
* Risk probability scores
* BI-consumable output tables

---

## 🔍 Use Case

The dataset models 1,500 tech professionals and explores:

* AI tool usage intensity
* Burnout levels
* Job satisfaction
* Fear of AI replacement
* Attrition risk classification (Low / Medium / High)

Primary objective:

> Predict employee attrition risk based on AI usage and wellbeing indicators.

---

## 🧠 Machine Learning Design

### Feature Engineering (Spark ML Pipeline)

* StringIndexer for categorical features
* OneHotEncoder
* StandardScaler for numeric features
* VectorAssembler
* Label encoding for target

Pipeline artifacts are persisted to Lakehouse for reproducibility.

---

### Models Trained

* Logistic Regression (baseline)
* Random Forest (non-linear ensemble model)

Models are:

* Trained on 80/20 split
* Evaluated using Accuracy & F1-score
* Persisted to Lakehouse storage
* Used for batch inference

---

## 🔁 Automated Retraining

A Fabric Data Pipeline orchestrates:

1. Silver transformation
2. Feature engineering
3. Model training
4. Batch scoring
5. Gold table refresh

The pipeline is:

* Parameterized
* Schedule-ready (e.g. monthly retraining)
* Executable on-demand

This simulates production-grade ML operations (MLOps-lite).

---

